Well, given the permutations that xorlo has gone through over the years since it 
became official, there were probably times when it was overtly bloburist, though 
the usual state seems to me to have been Readymadeist (if if you want to insist 
on a difference), as witness the introduction of plural reference, which was 
thought a big step forward.  Of course, I know that xorxes has always had 
inchoate and usually terribly ill-formed blobularist ideas in mind, but none of 
them ever eventuated in any of the "final" versions of xorlo and usually 
disappeared without a trace or with only the salvageable (readymadeist) parts.



